      "notes": [
        "*These drugs have a narcotic effect and may be addictive. Additional narcotic effects as follows:",
        "For Depressants, character receives –(Drug Strength ÷ 2) to WIL and RFL scores**",
        "For Stimulants, character receives –(Drug Strength ÷ 2) to DEX and +(0.25 x Drug Strength) to RFL**",
        "For Hallucinogens, character receives –(Drug Strength ÷ 2) to WIL score and Perception Skill, and –(0.25 x Drug Strength) to Compulsion/Paranoid Trait**",
        "**Round values down to a minimum of 0. If the drug modifi es a Trait the character does not otherwise have, the character receives that Trait while under the drug’s infl uence. Poison Notes: Lethal poisons inflict their Drug Strength as damage. Delayed poisons hold their effect until the end of the Duration period. Continuous poisons apply half their Drug Strength in damage every Duration until an anti-toxin is applied, or the victim dies."
      ]
